    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0323" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.M5/151</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-09">October 9, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        20.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1692</seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">L. N. No. 1824</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my telegram No. 96 dated
                    October 9, 10 a.m.,<anchor n="51" xml:id="d228-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith the letter of the Deputy Secretary General of the League of
                    Nations (C.L. 279 (c) 1930. II)<anchor n="52" xml:id="d228-f2"/> dated <pb
                        facs="0324" n="244" xml:id="pg244"/> October 8, 1930, whereby he informs you
                    that he has convened the States that participated in the Conference of
                    February–March 1930 to a second Conference of Concerted Economic Action to meet
                    at Geneva on November 17, 1930, and further points out that should the United
                    States Government desire to designate an official observer or other
                    representative to follow the proceedings of the Conference, as at the
                    February–March Conference, he would be glad to give him the necessary
                    facilities.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierrepont Moffat</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
